---
import Layout from '../components/layout/Layout.astro';
import ShowcaseBadge from '../components/layout/ShowcaseBadge.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="NovaFabric concepts — five primitives and replay modes"
  description="The five primitives, replay modes, and how they compose into replay and evidence infrastructure for agentic systems."
>
  <article class="container-content py-16 md:py-24">
    <header class="max-w-2xl">
      <ShowcaseBadge variant="page" />
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl md:text-5xl font-medium tracking-tight text-balance">Concepts</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">
        The five primitives, the five replay modes, and the boundaries that
        keep NovaFabric self-hosted and CLI-first.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="mt-16 container-prose space-y-10 text-[var(--color-text-muted)] leading-relaxed">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium text-[var(--color-text)] tracking-tight mb-3">Five primitives</h2>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">Asset Registry</strong> names every model, agent, prompt,
          tool, dataset, evaluation, and deployment with <code class="text-[var(--color-text)]">name@version</code>
          identity. Promotion from development to production is gated by eval suites that pass or fail.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          <strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">Run Capsule</strong> is a self-contained, schema-validated
          record of one AI run: the command, the model and tool calls capture can see, the environment, the
          assets referenced. Stored as a directory under <code class="text-[var(--color-text)]">~/.novafabric/capsules/&lt;ulid&gt;/</code>.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          <strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">Replay</strong> reconstructs a run under one of five modes
          with explicit guarantees. You always know what was real and what was reconstructed.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          <strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">Lineage</strong> is the causation graph that links runs to
          the assets they consumed and the artifacts they produced — answers "what depended on what" without
          guesswork.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          <strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">Evidence Bundle</strong> is the signed, portable proof of
          what happened: in-toto DSSE Statement v1, ed25519 signature, vendored schemas, a tamper-evident manifest hash.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="replay-modes">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium text-[var(--color-text)] tracking-tight mb-3">Five replay modes</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-3">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">exact</strong> — re-execute end-to-end. Available only
            for local models or fully containerized environments. Greyed out for remote LLMs because we will
            not pretend a remote API call is deterministic.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">mocked</strong> — re-execute the agent code, serve every
            model and tool call from the capsule's cache. Same control flow, same outputs, no network.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">semantic</strong> — re-execute, then a judge model
            compares meaning. Requires a judge model in real use. Useful for "did the meaning change?"
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">forensic</strong> — no re-execution. Read-only inspection
            of what the capsule recorded. The audit mode.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">intervention</strong> <em>(experimental)</em> —
            substitute one captured model/tool event and replay downstream under mocked semantics for
            counterfactual root-cause analysis.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium text-[var(--color-text)] tracking-tight mb-3">Why self-hosted</h2>
        <p>
          AI runs accumulate sensitive data: prompts, intermediate reasoning, internal documents pulled by
          tools. Shipping that to a hosted service means signing a DPA, picking a region, paying per GB,
          waiting for a backup window when audit asks. NovaFabric runs in your own infrastructure instead —
          on your machine for a single user, or in your own self-hosted server (server mode, with OIDC and
          RBAC) for teams. Your run data never leaves your environment unless you choose to move it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium text-[var(--color-text)] tracking-tight mb-3">Why CLI-first</h2>
        <p>
          The CLI remains the canonical automation surface and emits machine-readable output. NovaFabric
          also ships <code class="text-[var(--color-text)]">nova serve</code> for browser/dashboard workflows;
          v0.102.0 added scoped authorization and tenancy safety checks to that surface.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <footer class="mt-16 pt-8 border-t border-[var(--color-border)] text-sm text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">
      <p>
        Ready to try it? <a href="/install/" class="text-[var(--color-text)] underline underline-offset-4 decoration-[var(--color-border-strong)] hover:decoration-[var(--color-text)]">Install</a>,
        or explore the showcase: <a href="/showcase/lineage/" class="text-[var(--color-text)] underline underline-offset-4 decoration-[var(--color-border-strong)] hover:decoration-[var(--color-text)]">Lineage</a>.
      </p>
    </footer>
  </article>
</Layout>
